# nura-builds overlay (targets/s3ve3g.sh): pmaports' recipe at 6b904fc480
# (6.16.12-r4), copied over the pmaports recipe by scripts/setup.sh. Since 7.3.4: mainline (kernel.org)
# with msm8226-mainline's patch stack (its 56 commits on top of v6.16.12 in tag v6.16.12-msm8226-u2,
# ported to v7.3.4, rebased onto v7.3.6: patch 0000, one mbox with the commits), as
# msm8226-mainline has no newer branch. Changes are marked
# "nura-builds:": the Samsung Galaxy S III Neo's device tree (eMMC, SD card, USB, keys, touch,
# sensors, Wi-Fi, splash framebuffer; it had the serial port only), the ALSA sequencer, the
# YAS532 magnetometer and the Terminus 16x32 console font in the config; an early console into
# a RAM buffer (earlycon=ramcon,<address>: the log until a reset, read from TWRP as /proc/last_kmsg).
# The device options are built in (CONFIG_CMDLINE, appended to the bootloader's): Samsung's
# bootloader adds ~840 characters and refuses more than 1024 in total. Only for the S III Neo:
# earlycon=ramcon writes to RAM at 0x1FB00000. The USB switch (extcon-sm5502 on i2c-gpio) is built in:
# as modules it probed after the initramfs's USB gadget setup, which found no UDC and gave up.
# No DEBUG_INFO_BTF since 7.3.4 (the image has to stay small, see build()); with it went
# MODULE_ALLOW_BTF_MISMATCH. simpledrm built in: it holds the splash framebuffer's
# clocks and power domain from early on, and the console is on the screen before the initramfs.
# Co-Maintainer: Luca Weiss <luca@lucaweiss.eu>
maintainer="Stefan Hansson <newbyte@postmarketos.org>"
